=== graph (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Ask one question of the resolved call/type graph

Usage: ryii graph [OPTIONS] <--callers <[PATH#]NAME>|--uses <NAME>|--from <[PATH#]NAME>|--call-path <[PATH#]NAME>|--type-path <[PATH#]NAME>|--flow-path <BLOB@START:END>|--slice <PATH:BYTE>> [PATH]...

Arguments:
  [PATH]...  Files, directories, or globs; - reads a path list from stdin

Options:
      --fast-receivers <written>    Resolve written receiver types in fast mode
      --pattern <GLOB>              Keep files matching GLOB under each directory input; repeatable
      --entry <FILE>                Run on the files FILE reaches over imports (universe: the PATH inputs, else FILE's project)
      --depth <N>                   Import hops from --entry
      --root <DIR>                  Corpus root
      --callers <[PATH#]NAME>       Resolved call edges landing on NAME; PATH#NAME keeps NAME declared in files whose path ends with PATH
      --uses <NAME>                 Declarations that reference type NAME
      --from <[PATH#]NAME>          Everything NAME reaches along call edges; PATH#NAME seeds only NAME declared in files whose path ends with PATH
      --call-path <[PATH#]NAME>     Shortest call paths from NAME; PATH#NAME seeds only NAME declared in files whose path ends with PATH
      --type-path <[PATH#]NAME>     Shortest type-reference paths from NAME; PATH#NAME seeds only NAME declared in files whose path ends with PATH
      --flow-path <BLOB@START:END>  Flow paths from PATH@START:END or BLOB@START:END. START/END are zero-based UTF-8 byte offsets, END exclusive. PATH is read under --root (or the current directory); --at reads the revision. BLOB is the exact tagged content digest from file.digest or flow_edge.from_blob (blake3:HEX for worktree facts), not a bare git object ID. Follows local df edges and interprocedural flow_edge facts from the asked node only. --reverse answers what reaches the node
      --reverse                     Follow incoming value-flow edges to answer what reaches the seed
      --slice <PATH:BYTE>           Control-dependence slice at PATH:BYTE
      --sqlite <PATH>               Keep the fact store in a new SQLite database at PATH
      --slow                        Walk the SCIP oracle's edges (ryi slow) instead of the syntax resolve
      --timeout <SECS>              Seconds the question may run; past it graph exits 3 [default: 30]
      --at <REV>                    Query a committed revision
      --compare <REV>               Diff the answers against REV
      --scip-index <FILE>           Load this index.scip
      --rust-checker                Add rust-analyzer type evidence
      --ts-checker                  Add TypeScript checker type evidence
      --go-checker                  Add go/types type evidence
  -h, --help                        Print help
stderr:
=== cleave (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Move one item into another file, with its imports

Usage: ryii cleave [OPTIONS] [TARGET] [DEST]

Arguments:
  [TARGET]  SRC#ITEM (omit with --list)
  [DEST]    Destination file, created if missing (omit with --list)

Options:
      --list <LIST>      TSV of SRC#ITEM<TAB>DEST rows, applied in order as one stage
      --root <ROOT>      Corpus root (default: git root of SRC)
      --state <STATE>    Soopy state root, outside the corpus
      --drag             Also move private helpers only this item uses
      --slow             Use rust-analyzer for Rust and the TypeScript LSP for TS
      --commit           Apply instead of dry run
      --verify <VERIFY>  Command to run after --commit; failure rolls back
      --text-refs        Report leftover SRC spellings in plain text
      --json             End with one JSON line holding the plan
  -h, --help             Print help
stderr:
=== move (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Move a file and repair every specifier that names it

Usage: ryii move [OPTIONS] [OLD] [NEW]

Arguments:
  [OLD]  File to move (omit with --list)
  [NEW]  Destination

Options:
      --list <LIST>              TSV of old<TAB>new rows
      --root <ROOT>              Corpus root; repeatable
      --verify-cwd <VERIFY_CWD>  Directory --verify runs in (default: first root)
      --state <STATE>            Soopy state root, outside the corpus
      --commit                   Apply instead of dry run
      --shim                     Leave a reexport shim at OLD instead of rewriting importers
      --relocate-mod             Move a Rust module's `mod` line instead of adding #[path]
      --verify <VERIFY>          Command to run after --commit; failure rolls back
      --text-refs                Report leftover old-path spellings in plain text
  -h, --help                     Print help
stderr:
=== rename (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Rename a symbol and every occurrence bound to it

Usage: ryii rename [OPTIONS] [TARGET] [NEW]

Arguments:
  [TARGET]  FILE#OLD (omit with --list)
  [NEW]     New name

Options:
      --list <LIST>          TSV of anchor<TAB>old<TAB>new rows
      --root <ROOT>          Corpus root (default: git root of the first anchor)
      --state <STATE>        Soopy state root, outside the corpus
      --at <AT>              Byte offset of the declaration when OLD is declared twice
      --slow                 Plan with the compiler: the TypeScript 7 checker for TypeScript, rust-analyzer for Rust
      --commit               Apply instead of dry run
      --text-refs            Report leftover old-name spellings in plain text
      --verify-scip <INDEX>  SCIP index (default ROOT/index.scip): its seats join the plan
      --no-scip-merge        Only report the SCIP diff; keep the syntax plan as is
      --json                 End with one JSON line of abstains
  -h, --help                 Print help

Exit codes: 2 plan error, 3 ambiguous (pass --at), 4 not found, 5 inexact, 6 dynamic, 7 plan has abstains, 8 the --slow engine refused
stderr:
=== query (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Run a tree-sitter query over files

Usage: ryii query [OPTIONS] [PATH]...

Arguments:
  [PATH]...  Files, directories, or globs; - reads a path list from stdin

Options:
      --pattern <GLOB>   Keep files matching GLOB under each directory input; repeatable
      --entry <FILE>     Run on the files FILE reaches over imports (universe: the PATH inputs, else FILE's project)
      --depth <N>        Import hops from --entry
      --root <DIR>       Corpus root
      --lang <LANG>      Language name (default: from each file's extension)
      --query <QUERY>    Tree-sitter query text
      --scmpp <FILE>     scm++ query file: nested relations lowered to SQL over capture and CST rows
      --digest <DIGEST>  Expected content digest (one input only)
      --sqlite <PATH>    Write to a new SQLite database instead of stdout
      --timeout <SECS>   Seconds the scm++ run may take; past it query exits 3
  -h, --help             Print help
stderr:
=== region (exit 0) ===
stdout:
Replace a generated region between sprefa markers

Usage: ryii region [OPTIONS] <TARGET> <ID>

Arguments:
  <TARGET>  DL7 file holding the markers
  <ID>      Marker id after sprefa:auto-begin / sprefa:auto-end

Options:
      --generated <GENERATED>  Generated body file, or - for stdin [default: -]
      --apply                  Write the replacement (default: report drift)
      --state <STATE>          Soopy state root for --apply
  -h, --help                   Print help
